    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1684">

                <pb facs="1068" n="952" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg952"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/707.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 11.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 19, 1914.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department of State acknowledges the
                    receipt of your note of October 16, 1914, in which you state that the Nicaraguan
                    Government will not undertake to obtain from the Nicaraguan Congress
                    ratification of the proposed agreement with Messrs. Brown Brothers &amp; Company
                    and Seligman &amp; Company, postponing for four months the payment of interest
                    on the debt which the Government of Nicaragua owes to these bankers.</p>
                <p>The Department of State views with sympathy the efforts which the Nicaraguan
                    Government is making to arrange a difficult financial situation and will be
                    pleased to receive any further information that you desire to place before
                    it.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
